   "text": "Read DESIGN first. Create these 4 files from scratch, replacing the old index.html. Do not touch the kept modules.\n\n**site/index.html**\n- `lang=en`, viewport meta, title \"Polish Quest: finish your game, one prompt at a time\", meta description.\n- CSP meta: `default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'`. (frame-ancestors goes only in `_headers`.)\n- Link `css/app.css`.\n- Body, in this order:\n  - `<canvas id=\"bg\" aria-hidden=\"true\">`\n  - `<header class=\"bar\">`: `<a class=\"brand\" href=\"#home\">Polish Quest</a>`, then `<nav>` with links `#overview` \"All steps\", `#fix` \"Fix Kit\", `#privacy` \"Privacy\".\n  - `<div class=\"progress\"><i id=\"progress-fill\"></i></div>`\n  - `<main id=\"screen\" tabindex=\"-1\">`\n  - `<div id=\"toast\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">`\n  - `<input type=\"file\" id=\"file\" accept=\".zip\" class=\"hidden\">`\n  - `<noscript>` with one line.\n- Scripts, all with `defer`, in exactly this order:\n  - js/config.js, js/data.js, js/core.js\n  - js/prompts-1.js, js/prompts-2.js, js/prompts-3.js, js/prompts-4.js, js/prompts-fix.js\n  - js/zip.js, js/detect.js, js/store.js\n  - js/scene.bundle.js\n  - js/app.js, js/screens-steps.js, js/screens-more.js, js/guide.js, js/mascot.js\n- Later tasks create the missing files. app.js must work when they are absent.\n- No inline script and no `style` attributes.\n\n**site/_headers**\n- For `/*`:\n  - the same CSP plus `frame-ancestors 'none'`\n  - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`\n  - `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`\n  - `Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()`\n\n**site/css/app.css** (target under 11KB)\n- `@font-face` Inter: `url(../assets/fonts/inter-latin-wght-normal.woff2)`, weight 100 900, `font-display: swap`.\n- CSS variables for the DESIGN palette. Use only those 6 colors plus transparent/alpha versions of them.\n- `html, body`: height 100%, margin 0, bg, text, 17/26 Inter, `overflow: hidden`.\n- `#bg`: fixed, inset 0, full width and height, z-index 0.\n- `body.no3d #bg { display: none }`, and `body.no3d` gets `background: radial-gradient(circle at 75% 45%, rgba(255,197,61,.14), transparent 45%)` over the bg color.\n- `.bar`: fixed top, 56px, z 3, flex space-between, padding 0 24px.\n  - Brand: weight 700, 18px.\n  - Nav links: 15px, muted, min-height 44px, inline-flex centered, gap 20px.\n  - On phone (max-width 640px): padding 0 16px, gap 12px, 14px.\n- `.progress`: fixed, top 56px, height 3px, full width, line color. `#progress-fill` is accent, with a width transition of .4s.\n- `#screen`:\n  - position absolute, inset `59px 0 0 0`, z 1\n  - flex column, justify center\n  - padding `24px max(24px, 8vw)`\n  - `overflow-y: auto`, outline none\n  - Its direct child `.frame` has max-width 560px and enters with fade plus 12px rise over .35s.\n- Typography classes from DESIGN: `h1`, `h2`, `.kicker`, `.lead` (19/28, muted), `.muted`, small text at 14px.\n- `.btn`:\n  - min-height 52px, padding 0 22px, radius 12px\n  - 17px, weight 650\n  - border `1px solid var(--line)`, surface background, text color\n  - cursor pointer, inline-flex centered\n- `.btn-primary`: accent background, `#0B0D12` text, no border.\n- `.btn-ghost`: transparent.\n- `.btn:disabled`: opacity .5.\n- `.link`: a button styled as underlined text, min-height 44px.\n- `.actions`: flex, gap 12px, wrap, margin-top 28px.\n- `.chip`: min-height 44px, padding 0 16px, radius 22px, border line, 16px. `.chip[aria-pressed=true]`: accent border and accent text.\n- `.card`: surface, border line, radius 14px, padding 20px.\n- `.field`: input 52px tall, surface, border line, radius 12px, text color, 17px, padding 0 14px, width 100%.\n- `.row`: flex, space-between, align center, padding 14px 0, border-bottom line.\n- `.stack > * + *`: margin-top 16px.\n- `.tag`: 14px, accent text, accent border at .4 alpha, radius 8px, padding 4px 10px.\n- `.panel`: surface card, max-height 46vh, overflow auto, 15/24, `white-space: pre-wrap`, tabindex-focusable.\n- `.tiles`: grid, `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr))`, gap 10px. `.tile`: a button card, text left, min-height 64px. `.tile.is-done`: muted. `.tile.is-now`: accent border.\n- `.meter`: 6px bar in line color with an accent fill.\n- `#toast`: fixed, bottom 24px, left 50%, translated; surface, border accent, radius 12px, padding 12px 18px, z 6, opacity 0. `.show`: opacity 1.\n- `.hidden { display: none !important }`\n- `:focus-visible` ring per DESIGN.\n- Phone (max-width 640px):\n  - h1 30/36.\n  - `#screen`: padding 16px 16px 120px, `justify-content: flex-start`.\n  - `.actions`: fixed, left 0, right 0, bottom 0; padding 12px 16px; bg color at .92 alpha; border-top line; z 2. Buttons `flex: 1`.\n- `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`: no animations or transitions.\n- Guarantee no horizontal overflow: `max-width: 100%`, `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on headings.\n\n**site/js/app.js** (IIFE, target under 14KB)\n- Implements `window.PQ.app` exactly per the DESIGN contract.\n- Never uses innerHTML.\n- State:\n  - On boot, load `PQ.store.load()` inside try/catch into `state {scan, done: {}, core}`.\n  - `save()` calls `PQ.store.save(state)`.\n  - `ctx()` returns `PQ.makeCtx(state.scan)`.\n- Router (on `hashchange` and at boot):\n  - Parse `#name/param`; the default is `home`.\n  - If the route is one of `scan`, `step`, `done` and there is no `state.scan`, go to `#home`.\n  - Clear `#screen`, create `div.frame`, call the registered screen.\n  - If the screen is not registered (later tasks), render a placeholder frame: title \"Coming up\", plus a `.btn-primary` [data-t=next] that goes to the next logical route. Next logical route: `step/N` -> `step/N+1`, or `#done` after 26.\n  - Then:\n    - focus `#screen`\n    - set `#progress-fill` width to (count of done / 26)%\n    - call `window.PQ3D && PQ3D.setMood(mood)`, where mood is `home`, `scan`, `step`, `done`, or `quiet` for the other routes\n    - call `PQ3D.setProgress(doneCount / 26)` if that function exists\n    - dispatch `pq:route`\n- Boot, on DOMContentLoaded: call `PQ3D.start(document.getElementById('bg'))` inside try/catch. If there is no PQ3D, or it returns false, add `body.no3d`.\n- `toast(text)`: shows for 2.5s.\n- `copy(text)`: uses `navigator.clipboard.writeText`, with a fallback to a hidden textarea plus `execCommand`. Resolves true or false.\n- `frame(root, opts)`: builds kicker, h1, lead, a `div.stack` body and a `div.actions`. Returns `{body, actions}`.\n- Screen `home` (copy per DESIGN):\n  - Primary button [data-t=pick] clicks `#file`.\n  - `#file` change, or a drop on window, starts the scan. Call `preventDefault` on dragover and drop.\n  - Ghost [data-t=sample]: sets `state.scan = PQ.detect.sample()`, `done = {}`, saves, then `go('#scan')`.\n  - If there is a saved `state.scan`:\n    - primary is \"Continue {scan.name}, step {first not-done n}\" -> `#step/n`\n    - ghost \"Start over\" calls `PQ.store.clear()`, resets state and re-renders\n    - still show the [data-t=sample] button\n  - Scanning:\n    - hide the actions; show `.meter` and a status line\n    - call `PQ.detect.scan(file, {onProgress(stage, frac)})`\n    - map stages list/manifests/read/think/done to the DESIGN lines\n    - set mood `scan`\n    - on success: store the scan, save, `go('#scan')`\n    - on reject: show `err.message` in a `.card` with the title \"That did not work\" and bring the buttons back\n- Screen `scan` (copy per DESIGN):\n  - The body is a `.card` with four rows.\n  - Name row: an input `.field` bound to `scan.name`, with `maxlength` 60.\n  - Engine row:\n    - shows the label from `PQ.ENGINES` by `scan.engineId`\n    - a \"Change\" `.link` toggles a chip list of all `PQ.ENGINES`, with `scan.engineAlts` first if present\n    - picking a chip sets `engineId` and `engineSure = true`, saves, and re-renders the row\n    - if `!scan.engineSure`, the chips start open with the DESIGN note\n  - Type row: the same with `PQ.GENRES`, `genreId` and `genreSure`.\n  - Weakest device row: chips from `PQ.DEVICES`, setting `scan.deviceId` (default `PQ.DEFAULT_DEVICE`; handle it being either an id or an object).\n  - If `scan.isSample`, show the muted line: \"This is a made-up example game.\"\n  - Actions:\n    - `.btn-primary` [data-t=next] \"Yes, start\": sets `engineSure` and `genreSure` to true, saves, `go('#step/0')`\n    - ghost \"Use another zip\" -> `#home`"
  }
